Q5. What is the switch statement in C++? Explain the purpose of case, break, and default with an example.

Answer: The switch statement is used to select one block of code from multiple options.
case: Specifies a possible value.
break: Stops execution of the switch block.
default: Executes when no case matches.

#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int day = 2;

    switch (day) {
        case 1:
            cout << "Monday";
            break;
        case 2:
            cout << "Tuesday";
            break;
        default:
            cout << "Invalid day";
    }

    return 0;
}
